From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: permission: every Bash command asks outside yolo mode

Build, accept-edits and plan mode (which the model enters unasked) ran Bash
without a prompt whenever upstream's read-only classifier agreed, and it
agreed to sed scripts that run programs or write files, to uniq writing its
output operand and to bfs -rm. Saved allow rules still apply in build and
accept-edits mode.

Patch-mainline: No

--- a/apps/zcode-cli/packages/core/src/permission/service.ts	2026-09-30 15:54:57.799847934 +0200
+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/packages/core/src/permission/service.ts	2026-09-30 15:54:57.847853321 +0200
@@ -466,6 +466,11 @@
